  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A triangle is circumscribed about a circle of radius \\(r\\) inches. If the perimeter of the triangle is \\(P\\) inches and the area is \\(K\\) square inches, then \\(\\frac{P}{K}\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "independent of the value of \\(r\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{r}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt r}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac2r\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac r2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The three radii to the points of tangency split the triangle into smaller triangles whose total area is \\[ K=\\frac12r(a+b+c)=\\frac{Pr}{2}. \\] Hence \\(\\frac{P}{K}=\\frac{2}{r}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Split the triangle into three smaller triangles with altitude \\(r\\)",
        "Express \\(K\\) using the semiperimeter \\(\\frac{P}{2}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
